Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"brainfreeze|...Nobody ever warmed me up before. Take the scoops. They're in the freezer. Where scoops go.":"","grace|All nine. Still perfect. And MOO-RIELLE. You were on a FREEZER. We'll talk about it later.":"","brainfreeze|I'll bring the ice. I'm mostly ice.":"","justin|Hold this. No, the other end. It's the OTHER banner. Don't touch the copper.":"","pip|My rock says happy birthday. He's on the counter. Please don't frost him.":"","deedee|He's a guest, Boppy. Sit. He can sit next to you. You could use the cold on that knee.":"","brainfreeze|That's a happy hum.":"","pistachio|Cones for everybody. And... hey, old friend. Happy birthday. I'm sorry it took twenty years.":"","grace|I'm not telling. That's the rule. I didn't make the rule.":"","brainfreeze|...This is a good birthday. I'm putting it on my door.":"","tom|Hold on. It's your mom.":"","amy|Oh! Penny called. She's got birthday things for you at the shop, Grace. Three of them. On the house.":"","amy|Tom. Don't panic. I'm panicking enough for both of us.":"","grace|MOM. It's fine. I'll invite them myself. I'm very persuasive.":"","amy|Grace's friends are in the Square. Pip, Moss and Dot. Hand them out. By HAND. Like it's 1994.":"","grace|Pip! My party. Today. Four o'clock. There's a sundae with NINE scoops.":"","pip|Can my rock come? He's never been to a party.":"","pip|He gets nervous around cake. He'll be fine. He's a rock.":"","pip|Then we'll be there. Both of us. He'll bring a gift. It's a smaller rock.":"","dot|I'll count the guests. Somebody has to.":"","moss|Also, the tree says a freezer went north this morning. Humming. It wasn't happy.":"","dot|Nine years. Nine scoops. Nine candles. That's twenty-seven nines. I'll be there.":"","pip|I'm taking my pet rock for a walk.":"","pip|He's shy. Please don't make eye contact.":"","pip|Excellent. He's already learned 'stay'.":"","moss|I think I'm barking up the wrong tree.":"","dot|I've counted them seventeen times.":"","dot|I had to start all over. I'm at four hundred and six.":"","gus|I'm training for the annual sit-down.":"","dot|Tomorrow I'm moving on to windows.":"","bean|I didn't stop it. I collect wrong turns, not pies.":"","bean|I'm not lost. I'm collecting wrong turns.":"","gus|Your father caught Old Iron-Gill? And let him GO? Forty years of telling that story, and now it's true.":"","gus|Bait shack is open. Worms, minnows, and a sandwich I'm not selling.":"","michael|Principal Pruitt. Thirty-one years at Long Island Elementary. I've seen everything. Not tonight, though. Tonight is new.":"","bean|I cried a little. In the minivan. Don't tell Marco.":"","bean|I'm Marco’s dad. Marco says Mrs. Gregori is the toughest teacher in the whole school.":"","bean|Marco also says she's his favorite. Please don't tell Marco I told you.":"","oolong|Tell Mrs. Gregori her bulletin board is the best in the building. Don't tell the other teachers.":"","gus|They fixed the bells! In my lifetime! I'm going to tell everyone at the diner.":"","gus|I'm here for my grandson. He's in the second grade. I was in the second grade here in 1956.":"","justin|Conference night is over. I survived. I'm going to sit on this couch until Field Day.":"","justin|Deedee’s plate? Oh, everybody waits for Deedee’s plate. She brings one every conference night.":"","justin|Don't tell Gary. Gary eats the whole thing.":"","justin|Halverson. Fourth grade. I'm hiding in the staff room. That's allowed. It's in the contract.":"","justin|If you're hungry, the fridge is a minefield. Every lunch in there has a name on it. Read the labels.":"","bun|Today's special is yesterday's tomorrow toast.":"","page|It's quiet. Properly quiet. The good kind. Thank you, Tom.":"","page|The Stacks are through the staff door. Please be careful. And please don't answer the books.":"","page|I'm fine. Everything is fine. The dictionaries haven't slept in a week.":"","fern|They're all called Steve. It saves time.":"","page|It's fine. Everything is fine. Please whisper.":"","page|...Did you hear that? That wasn't me. I'd know my own shush.":"","luna|There's supposed to be a full moon tonight. My telescope can't find it.":"","luna|The moon is back. I looked at it for an hour. I didn't even write anything down.":"","oolong|I told it to mind its own business. It's a kettle. It has no business.":"","luna|I've discovered a new constellation.":"","luna|It's shaped exactly like my laundry.":"","penny|Welcome to Penny's Pockets. I sell things for pockets. Also things for people.":"","sal|I have one cab. It's cab seven. Cabs one through six are a dream I'm working on.":"","justin|Tom. Hey. Hold this. No, the other end. Don't touch the copper.":"","justin|Grace, Rose, come here. Who's Daddy's favorite? Both. Correct. Go get 'em.":"","justin|Long Island born. Country music raised. Don't ask me how. Nobody knows.":"","justin|Big game tonight. If you hear yelling, that's me. If you hear crying, that's also me.":"","justin|Watch your step, Tom. That board is loose. I know. It's on the list.":"","amy|Tom. Thank you for coming. You're the good uncle. By a lot.":"","amy|Justin says the hallway light is almost done. It's been almost done since June.":"","amy|Did Boppy give you that cap? Don't let him near the pond.":"","amy|Rose. Big feelings are allowed. Throwing Lamby isn't. Come here.":"","deedee|The tomatoes are coming in. You're going home with forty.":"","amy|Grace, you don't have to be the best at it. You have to be the one who keeps going. Okay, now be the best at it.":"","deedee|Boppy says he's not feeling good. Boppy also won't stop fishing.":"","deedee|A little glass of wine with dinner. Just one. Nurse's orders.":"","deedee|Rhubarb crisp is cooling on the counter. Don't touch it. Okay, one corner.":"","ellie|The girls and I are playing cards. I'm winning. I'm also cheating. They're learning a great deal.":"","ellie|I had a date with a man who turned out to be a disappointment. The coat wasn't. Keep it warm for me.":"","ellie|Tom. Stand up straight. There. Now you look like someone I'm related to.":"","ellie|Deedee keeps offering me rhubarb crisp. I keep saying yes. That's called manners.":"","ellie|I've been to Paris eleven times. Long Island is charming. Like a hat you wear once.":"","ellie|Yes, Deedee has an aunt. Yes, I'm older. No, you may not ask by how much.":"","ellie|Deedee says I'm sharp. I say everyone else is a little dull.":"","boppy|At Rikers we did headcounts. Grace, one. Rose, two. Tom, you're dragging.":"","boppy|Tom! Good. I'm not feeling good. Something with the stomach. Sit, I'll tell you about it.":"","boppy|I'm not feeling good. I was fine an hour ago. Then I had a pepper.":"","boppy|Did I tell you about the championship race? I did? Sit down. I'll tell you again.":"","boppy|Deedee says I'm not allowed near the pond. The pond says otherwise.":"","bun|I'm filming a day-in-my-life video. I live in the lofts.":"","bun|This is the day. You're in my life now.":"","boppy|Grace, Rose, who's the strongest grandpa? Correct. Now help me up.":"","bean|I'm an actor. Well. I'm an actor who parks cars at a tower.":"","page|I'm a screenwriter. I live in the lofts, two floors down from your boyfriend.":"","page|Draft forty-one. It's about a man who writes screenplays. It's very personal.":"","boomie2|Friday is the home show, right here downtown. You're in the front row. I wrote your name on the seat.":"","page|He lends me a mug when I'm stuck. I'm stuck a lot. I have nine of his mugs.":"","boomie2|Oh, the sun's coming up on my street. Hallelujah, hallelujah! Sorry. I sang that whole sentence.":"","boomie2|Atlanta, then Chicago, then Nashville. I keep saying it out loud so I don't forget.":"","boomie2|Friday night, front row. I don't start the show without you. Okay, I start. But I look for you.":"","boomie2|How's TNB? Tell him there's a seat for him too. Two front row seats. Don't make me beg.":"","boomie2|Oh, when the morning comes, I'm gonna rise. Rise, rise, rise! Sing with me, Tom. Amen!":"","boomie2|I open with a hymn my grandmother sang. She'd say I'm doing it too loud. She'd be right.":"","boomie2|Sol says he parks his cab outside to hear me warm up. I say he's just early.":"","boomie2|Hmm hmm hmmm. Oh, I was humming? I'm always humming.":"","olivia|Nara ate! A whole plate! Off your plate, but still! I'm counting it!":"","olivia|Michael, Isla has a roll in each hand. That's fine. That's a balanced meal.":"","olivia|Nara slept! Twelve hours! She's snoring like Michael.":"","olivia|My lasagna is a brick. A cold lasagna brick. Michael is holding it. He's holding everything.":"","olivia|Is she okay? Is she eating? She's not eating, is she.":"","olivia|Michael, the squirrel is back on the fence. Don't make eye contact.":"","olivia|Tom! You kept Nara alive! Did she eat? She didn't eat, did she.":"","olivia|Tom! Hi! Sorry, I'm mid-sentence in my head. I'm filing a story on AI in classrooms.":"","olivia|My editor wants a piece on AI taking jobs. I said I'd write it myself. While I still can.":"","olivia|Michael, can you take Lachlan? He's licking the fence. Thank you, babe.":"","olivia|Everybody asks if robots will take their jobs. I tell them a robot still can't fold a fitted sheet. Neither can I.":"","olivia|I interviewed a chatbot today. It was very polite. Too polite. I didn't trust it.":"","olivia|Teachers aren't getting replaced. They're getting a very confident new student who never did the reading.":"","michael|I have Isla, the diaper bag, and a cold lasagna. I'm at full capacity.":"","michael|Hey, Tom. I'd wave, but I'm out of arms.":"","michael|Lachlan got his truck back. He hasn't put it down. He's eating cereal with one hand.":"","michael|I work at Meta. I build things that connect people. Right now I'm connecting a four-year-old to a nap.":"","michael|I heard Olivia say Michael. I'm already holding them. I'm always holding them.":"","michael|Yes, Olivia. Got him. Got her. Got both. I've had both since breakfast.":"","michael|My arms have never been stronger. I haven't lifted a weight in four years.":"","washington|That coat looks right on you. My daddy would say so. Then he'd say stand up straight.":"","michael|Lachlan wants to know if Nara is his dog. I said it's complicated. It's not. It's his dog.":"","washington|Forty loaves. I ate four. Don't tell Bernadette.":"","washington|Forty years I've made gumbo for this potluck. Today the stove won't light. The flame just leans. Toward the boulevard.":"","washington|You're the one fixing up the green house? Keep the old windows. They're better than the new ones.":"","washington|That smog had me stuck on one sentence for an hour. At my age I don't have hours to spare.":"","la_woman|My dog ate a whole loaf. I found him. He was under the table. He's always under the table.":"","la_woman|There he is. No. That's a squirrel. It's looking at me.":"","la_woman|My tamales are cold. My dog is cold. My dog is somewhere. He's probably cold.":"","la_woman|I'm walking my dog. I've always been walking my dog.":"","la_woman|I'm walking my dog. He's somewhere.":"","la_woman|I'll always be walking my dog. Isn't that nice?":"","la_woman|There he is. No. That's a lemon.":"","la_woman|My grandparents rented on this block. Now I rent on this block. We're a tradition.":"","gus|It's a whole system. Their system is better.":"","gus|I'm blowing leaves. The squirrels keep blowing them back.":"","gus|I'm blowing leaves. The same leaf. Over and over.":"","gus|I'm blowing leaves.":"","gus|Tomorrow, they blow them back. It's a whole system.":"","moss|Good job, Tom. Don't tell anyone I said good job.":"","dot|I'm going to sleep for a week. In my car. With the headset on.":"","moss|Nobody gets past Ray. Except the dog. The dog got past Ray. Don't tell anyone.":"","dot|If anybody asks, I'm walking somewhere important. I'm always walking somewhere important.":"","la_woman|Without wardrobe there's no shoot. Without a shoot there's no movie.":"","la_woman|Without a movie I go back to directing car commercials. I love cars. I don't love talking cars.":"","la_woman|Dana Park. Director. First feature. Please don't ask me how it's going.":"","penny|Case closed. I've filed my report. With myself. I approved it.":"","penny|You're a good neighbor, Tom. So is the dog. Mostly the dog.":"","penny|Except squirrels. I'm working on it.":"","penny|Then the tree. There's a knock. I have only ever heard parts of it.":"","penny|Welcome to Nickel's. I'm Penny's cousin. Better weather, same prices.":"","oolong|You're Tom? TNB's Tom! He found a shoe for us once. A lead actor's shoe. Four minutes before the take.":"","oolong|We still talk about the shoe. Tell him there's always a rack here with his name on it.":"","sal|Angel City Cab Co. I'm Sol. Sal's cousin. Also one cab.":"","sal|Cab eight. Sal has cab seven. We don't talk about what happened to the other six.":"","carmen|Everybody says, 'Mama, the house is so full of love.' It's full of SOMETHING. Take tamales. Please. I need the room in my fridge.":"","carmen|Tony, feet off my table! Kevin, the baby isn't a football! Mateo, give Abuela the remote! ...Tom, mijo, sit. If you can find a chair.":"","moss|I've been in this chair since the game started. Which game? Yes.":"","michael|Me and Yesenia are saving for our own place. In this market? We'll be here until Mateo goes to college.":"","michael|The two houses next door sold for more than this whole block cost in 1990. My mom isn't okay about it.":"","la_woman|Baby Lupita is finally asleep. If you wake her, you're moving in.":"","bean|I share the bunk bed with Uncle Tony's exercise bike.":"","luna|Night shift nurse. I sleep in the bathtub. It's the only room with a lock.":"","bean|It's not a metaphor. The bike is on the top bunk.":"","rose|I'm making a documentary about this house. It's a horror movie.":"","rose|Scene one: the bathroom line. Scene two: who ate Abuela's last concha.":"","rose|I'm a dinosaur. RAWR.":"","rose|Abuela says no more dinosaurs inside. I'm a quiet dinosaur. rawr.":"","tnb|Go on, I'll be right here. I'm pot-sitive about it.":"","tnb|Took the longboard down Spring Street this morning. Smooth. There's a crack by Fourth Street I've named.":"","tnb|Watered your plants on 2nd Ave. The fern asked about you. I said you're fine.":"","dot|34th floor. From my desk I can see Griffith Park. I've never been to Griffith Park.":"","odette|The gumbo never has to be done, baby. Isn't that nice? Nothing ever has to be done.":"","odette|Sit down, baby. Gumbo's on. It's been on since six.":"","carmen|Don't tell the juice bar. They'll want the recipe.":"","carmen|Bienvenidos! Pupusas revueltas, and curtido on the side. Curtido isn't optional.":"","kit|Have you tried the juice bar on Jefferson? It's so nice the neighborhood is finally getting... options.":"","pip|Mrs. Alvarez brought us tamales. We posted them. We tagged her. She doesn't have Instagram.":"","pip|Our mortgage is, um. We don't say the number out loud. The house can hear.":"","dot|We're restoring the original 1912 windows. It's a whole thing.":"","bean|Baby Hudson is asleep. Please whisper. Please. I'm begging.":"","mudling|I have a sprout. Don't touch my sprout.":"","mudling|Blub. You're big. I'm mud.":"","mudling|...I'm a puddle now. Give me a minute.":"","grump|Grrrumble. You're standing in my puddle.":"","mudling|The sprout is fine. I'm fine. Everything is fine.":"","skeeter|We're down to four skeeters. Come back when we're a swarm.":"","grump|...I'm thinking about my choices.":"","grump|Come back in a bit. I'll have new ones.":"","log|I rolled over. That's my whole warm-up.":"","log|I was a tree. Now I'm a nap with a face.":"","toad|Don't kiss me. I know what you've heard. Don't.":"","log|Moss is growing on me. I'm letting it.":"","bigone|GLUB. So you're the ones Boppy keeps talking about.":"","bigone|I've been in this pond since 1994. I've never been caught. I'll never be caught.":"","bigone|The pond is deep. I'll be in it.":"","mudling|I came from a tailpipe on the 101. I'm very proud.":"","mudling|...I'm waiting for rush hour. Then I'll be back.":"","skeeter|Street cleaning. Tuesday. Eight to ten. You didn't read the sign.":"","skeeter|We're seventy-three dollars each. There are a lot of us.":"","grump|I live here. You're visiting. Remember that.":"","skeeter|We're being processed. Come back in six to eight weeks.":"","grump|I've been running the fire roads.":"","grump|...I'm lying in the sun. Leave me alone.":"","grump|Come back after dark. I'm better after dark.":"","grump|You're in my lane. Everyone is in my lane.":"","grump|I'm parked. Leave a note.":"","grump|...SigAlert. Don't come this way.":"","mudling|Glorp. I've had mammoths. You're not a mammoth.":"","mudling|I'm resting. Like a fossil.":"","bigone|RUMBLE. Everyone says I'm overdue.":"","bigone|I'm settling. Don't stand near the bookshelves.":"","bigone|I've been under this city for a million years. Nobody has ever been ready.":"","bigone|Rumble. I moved two inches. That's a lot for me.":"","mudling|...I'm drying. Don't look at me.":"","toad|I watch the water all day. The water doesn't watch back.":"","toad|...Bob. Bob. I'm resting. Bob.":"","grump|...I'm untangling. This could take years.":"","grump|Don't pull. Pulling makes it worse.":"","grump|Snarl. Somebody cast me badly in 1997. I've been in a knot ever since.":"","log|I'm soaking. I'm always soaking.":"","bigone|BLORP. I'm older than the pier. I'm older than the old man.":"","bigone|Blorp. I'm still burping peppers.":"","bigone|The pool is deep. I'll be at the bottom of it.":"","grump|They said there'd be a hot lunch. It was a cold sandwich.":"","grump|I'm back. They reset the scene.":"","grump|I've been an extra in forty movies. You've seen the back of my head forty times.":"","grump|I'm Man in Coat Number Four. They never call Number Four.":"","skeeter|Bzzz. I'm back in frame.":"","skeeter|...Fuzz. I'm fuzzy. Leave me alone.":"","toad|...Snap. I'm resting between takes.":"","mudling|...Hazy. I'm feeling hazy.":"","toad|Scene four, take nine. Don't ask about the other eight.":"","mudling|Don't look at me. You can't see me anyway.":"","grump|...I'm rewriting my cards.":"","bigone|Forty years of bad takes. I've heard every one of them. Through me.":"","skeeter|Nobody ever studies for me. That's the whole point of me. It's still rude.":"","skeeter|...I'm all multiple choice inside.":"","log|I'm not the one who's late. I'm just the one who says so.":"","mudling|...Drying. Don't touch me. I'm drying.":"","mudling|You'll be finding me in your hair until June.":"","toad|Every kid in this school is scared of me. I didn't ask for that.":"","toad|...Boing. I'm resting. Boing.":"","skeeter|You didn't see me. I was never here.":"","skeeter|I'm just an acorn. With sunglasses. That's all you need to know.":"","mudling|Everybody touches the tree and then says EW. I'm the tree.":"","mudling|I'm not sticky. I'm committed.":"","mudling|Give me a hundred years. I'll be amber.":"","skeeter|Nobody looks twice at a stick. That's the job. It's lonely.":"","skeeter|Report to the Chairman: they're very tall.":"","skeeter|...It's an acorn.":"","log|Nobody ever came back to finish. I've been folded for forty years.":"","log|I'm the corner of page 212. Somebody stopped reading here in 1987.":"","grump|I'm volume K. I know everything that starts with K.":"","toad|Nobody opens me anymore. I've been ready to pop for six years.":"","toad|I'm supposed to be the surprise.":"","mudling|Don't smell me. I'm serious. Don't.":"","mudling|Somebody said they'd eat me tomorrow. That was a long tomorrow.":"","log|Now there's nothing left to put out. So I put out the fun.":"","skeeter|Ironbelly asked for the flames. I just carried them. I'm a delivery draft.":"","skeeter|Close a window. Go on. I'll find another one.":"","skeeter|...wooo. Wooooo. That's me. I'm the wooo.":"","skeeter|...name? Your name. It's not here.":"","toad|...ew. Ew. Is that touching? It's touching. EW.":"","grump|I was ironed in 1971. I've stayed ironed.":"","log|I have held on for fifty-five years. That's my whole job. Holding on.":"","log|A lady left this coat with me in 1971. She said she'd be right back.":"","log|...ticket seven. I'm holding ticket seven.":"","log|She said she'd be right back. 1971.":"","mudling|I'm not shy. I'm just very, very good at walls.":"","mudling|...I'm fine here. By the wall. With the wall.":"","toad|I've been packed since 1989. Nobody ever came to pick me up.":"","toad|Twenty-two inches. I'm exactly twenty-two inches.":"","toad|Everybody says I'm too big. I'm just very prepared.":"","log|I'm very long. I'm very, very good at being long.":"","skeeter|Every clock in here says midnight. I've been tired since 1989.":"","mudling|I have sixty stickers. I've been everywhere. Nobody came to get me.":"","mudling|I've gone round this carousel since 1989. Every bag got picked up. Not me.":"","grump|I got here first. In 1989. I've been saving these seats ever since.":"","bigone|I've called it every night since. Somebody has to answer.":"","bigone|Midnight. It's always midnight. That way nobody is late.":"","sal|Cab seven needs new brakes. She's parked until the part comes in.":"","sal|Airport? On conference night? Your sister would find me. She'd find me on foot. Fast.":"","sal|He said, and I quote, \"tell him it's a bread emergency.\" I didn't know bread could have those.":"","sal|I don't know what that means. It sounded serious.":"","sal|Airport? You just got here. Your niece called the depot. From her mother’s phone.":"","sal|Airport? Every clock in town says midnight. The planes aren't going anywhere.":"","amy|Is that the Grump? I could take him. I've taken a second-grade class on a field trip.":"","deedee|I packed cookies. They're in my purse. The purse is at home. We go back.":"","deedee|When we get home I'm making a big dinner. Nobody argue.":"","tnb|After this, clay. Any two colors. I'll make them get along.":"","tnb|If a coyote jumps out at us, I've seen this movie. Stay together. Nobody go in the basement.":"","grace|Are we there yet? Where's there?":"","rose|I found a rock. It's a pet now.":"","amy|Go. I'll race you when you get back. And I'll win.":"","boppy|Go on. The recliner and I'll hold down the fort.":""});
Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.voices,{"amy":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"heavy Long Island accent","designed":false,"voice_id":"HLSHrV3D7Gp6sEFcHNev","name":"AoT Amy (Kind)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8}},"rose":{"voice_id":"ocZQ262SsZb9RIxcQBOj","name":"Lulu Lolipop - High-Pitched and Bubbly  (female, young, american, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"grace":{"voice_id":"i4CzbCVWoqvD0P1QJCUL","name":"Ivy","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":false},"deedee":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":false,"voice_id":"IvqgMRxvpv712BL3gkv5","name":"AoT Deedee (Long Island, 2026-10-28)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85}},"boppy":{"voice_id":"QzTKubutNn9TjrB7Xb2Q","name":"Jerry B. - New York Italian Mobster  (male, middle_aged, new york, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":1},"direction":"deep gravelly voice","designed":false},"sal":{"voice_id":"gcJ5PkVgShIxtP5HgbZK","name":"AoT Sal","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his fifties with a thick Long Island New York accent, a slightly nasal, raspy, fast and friendly voice. Chatty taxi driver, warm and a little dramatic, proud of his one cab. Clean studio recording."},"log":{"voice_id":"DmA9AOv6Fsic2LQdqVVM","name":"AoT Log Lump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A sleepy cartoon log creature, very slow, deep, woody and drowsy voice, yawning between words, mumbly and content. Animated character voice."},"tom":{"voice_id":"cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal","name":"Eric - Smooth, Trustworthy","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"bigone":{"voice_id":"qDteMRfOWoUEc7kcfWvl","name":"AoT The Big One","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An enormous ancient cartoon pond fish, huge slow booming bass voice with gurgling bubbles, pompous and boastful but childlike and easily delighted underneath. Animated character voice."},"toad":{"voice_id":"jcb48kKcDpNXjAxnAP2c","name":"AoT Bog Toad","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A huge cartoon toad, deep croaky throaty voice with a rumbling ribbit, territorial and proud, a bit vain. Animated character voice."},"skeeter":{"voice_id":"3NkCp1SubvPIw3g0s7Rf","name":"AoT Skeeter Swarm","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon swarm of mosquitoes speaking as one, high-pitched, thin, whiny and buzzy voice with a nasal zzz on every s, nosy and impatient. Animated character voice."},"tnb":{"voice_id":"QPmHuIriDGOvu1d9U7wn","name":"SuperDale - a mid-age voice & Friendly  (male, middle_aged, us midwest, informative_educational)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"boomie":{"voice_id":"FgGtmhYdBou3a14mKYgx","name":"AoT Boomie","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a big, warm, rich singer’s voice, bubbly and motherly, slides into song mid-sentence, laughs from the belly. Clean studio recording."},"bean":{"voice_id":"zROpM0X5rfQMe4CN4C7f","name":"AoT Bean","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his late twenties with an upbeat, rambling, friendly American voice. A little scattered, quick bursts of words, cheerful and unbothered. Light and bright. Clean studio recording."},"carmen":{"voice_id":"8ncJvaxiyfELP457mBLS","name":"AoT Doña Carmen","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her sixties with a warm, firm, proud voice and a light Salvadoran Spanish accent. Runs a pupuseria, generous and no-nonsense, laughs easily. Clean studio recording."},"pistachio":{"voice_id":"LyoSZrqTSG25l7i0uBGl","name":"AoT Mr. Pistachio","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his late fifties with a warm, hearty Long Island New York accent, an ice cream shop owner who loves his regulars, booming friendly laugh, talks with his hands, a little dramatic about his scoops. Clean studio recording."},"mudling":{"voice_id":"E2hOWZ8x3nGJuQURP3SG","name":"AoT Mudling","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small, silly cartoon creature made of mud, gloopy gurgling voice with wet bubbly consonants, slow and sulky, childlike and a little sad. Animated character voice."},"brainfreeze":{"voice_id":"kYM9iwUI7t87mhAOBs1T","name":"AoT Brain Freeze","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon villain who is a walking chest freezer: a flat, cold, humming monotone with a slight metallic buzz, deadpan and sulky, slow and heavy, with a lonely sadness underneath that cracks through when he is surprised. Animated character voice."},"boomie2":{"voice_id":"rrjdoujYPDo3FGeRqm3Q","name":"AoT Boomie","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A young Black American woman in her late thirties to early fourties with a warm, rich, low alto voice, smooth and a little husky, deeper than most women’s voices. A gospel and soul singer, kind and bubbly, laughs from the belly, slides into song mid-sentence. Clean studio recording."},"grump":{"voice_id":"moX2FuSiiLmOw0uEq4OU","name":"AoT Pond Grump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A grumpy cartoon swamp creature, low gravelly grumbling voice, cranky and wet-sounding, easily offended, a big softie underneath. Animated character voice."},"dot":{"voice_id":"gYzudf4C0nXnEecqXK5t","name":"AoT Dot","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small woman in her forties with a quick, crisp, precise American voice, slightly nasal. Talks fast in short exact phrases like she is reading a tally sheet. Proud of her accuracy. Clean studio recording."},"la_woman":{"voice_id":"eLXwnyHT9UJHbuyheJ9m","name":"AoT LA neighbor (woman)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her early thirties with a relaxed, warm, slightly husky Los Angeles voice. Easygoing, wry, a little tired, friendly neighbor energy. Clean studio recording."},"michael":{"voice_id":"24fSFWvKYGI0zVR7L6JQ","name":"AoT Michael","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A tall man in his early forties with a calm, low, dry American voice. A tech dad holding two kids, patient, deadpan, quietly funny, a little tired. Clean studio recording."},"penny":{"voice_id":"C0jocNoR6bwrjLXwelto","name":"AoT Penny","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a fast-talking, bright, enthusiastic American saleswoman voice. Quick patter, playful, warm and a little pushy, every line a pitch. Clean studio recording."},"page":{"voice_id":"UnNThlnnIcLaHiWDpFdl","name":"AoT Page","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his forties, a librarian with a hushed, dry, whispery American voice. Speaks very quietly and precisely, mildly scandalized by everything, droll. Soft breathy whisper. Clean studio recording."},"olivia":{"voice_id":"3KdkB2LF6PUw0muuS0j7","name":"AoT Olivia","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her late thirties with a quick, bright, articulate American voice. A journalist and mom of two little kids, talks fast, wry and warm, always half distracted. Clean studio recording."},"luna":{"voice_id":"qCj5kMANfHcvCnzG1gVB","name":"AoT Luna","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her thirties with a dreamy, slow, wonder-filled American voice. Soft and spacey, drifting pauses, sincere awe with a touch of embarrassment. Clean studio recording."},"justin":{"voice_id":"Pp9gl3BrnVq62dIWU2sx","name":"AoT Justin (Long Island)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his early forties with an easygoing, friendly voice, Long Island born with a slight country twang. Goofy proud dad, handyman, sports fan, relaxed and warm, quick to laugh. Clean studio recording."},"gus":{"voice_id":"CcabrpeMRBXae9HlsCuq","name":"AoT Gus","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An old man in his seventies with a slow, warm, slightly creaky American voice. Deadpan and dignified, treats sitting on a bench like serious athletic training. Unhurried. Clean studio recording."},"oolong":{"voice_id":"2PhKaj7sDKqdDEhqQyhl","name":"AoT Oolong","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly woman in her seventies with a warm, gossipy, conspiratorial voice and a light British accent. Leans in to share secrets, little cackle of a laugh, cozy and sly. Clean studio recording."},"washington":{"voice_id":"ARRjeRIXQjOrcraWRDoq","name":"AoT Mr. Washington","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly man in his eighties with a deep, warm, slow voice and a gentle hint of Louisiana in it. A neighborhood storyteller on his porch, unhurried, kind, a little gravelly. Clean studio recording."},"ellie":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":true,"voice_id":"hZCpO8frcjUSQcVVhRiz","name":"AoT Aunt Ellie (Long Island, 2026-10-28)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85}}});
